  "title": "Unit vector flows",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture For every graph $G$ without a bridge, there is a flow $\\phi: E(G) \\rightarrow S^2 = \\{ x \\in {\\mathbb R}^3: |x| = 1 \\}$.\n\nConjecture There exists a map $q:S^2 \\rightarrow \\{-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4\\}$ so that antipodal points of $S^2$ receive opposite values, and so that any three points which are equidistant on a great circle have values which sum to zero.",
